\begin{abstract}
We present the formal design, mathematical formulation, and numerical architecture of the
\textbf{Sovereign Simulation Engine (SSE)}, a unified multi-scale computational framework engineered
to model extreme astrophysical environments ($\rho > 10^{9}\,\mathrm{g/cm^3}$,
$B > 10^{12}\,\mathrm{G}$). Traditional astrophysical simulations rely on modular, decoupled
pipelines—separating stellar evolution, magnetohydrodynamics, nuclear reaction networks, and
radiation transport—which introduce secular energy drifts and synchronization errors across highly
non-linear phase transitions. The Sovereign Architecture solves the fully coupled, covariant system
of Einstein–Magnetohydrodynamic field equations simultaneously in real-time, integrating relativistic
degenerate-matter equations of state, high-resolution shock-capturing (HRSC) Riemann solvers, stiff
alpha-chain nuclear networks, and two-moment neutrino transport. This paper details the governing
continuum equations, Valencia formulation conservations, constrained transport divergence eradication,
and distributed hardware-accelerated execution pipelines required for stable, production-grade
continuum simulations.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction and Architectural Motivation}

The modeling of compact objects—core-collapse supernovae, neutron star mergers, magnetar
magnetospheres—requires simultaneous treatment of disparate physical regimes:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Strong-field General Relativity (3+1 ADM spacetime evolution)
\item Relativistic Magnetohydrodynamics (GRMHD) with extreme magnetization ($\beta \ll 1$)
\item Quantum-mechanical degenerate-matter pressures (relativistic and non-relativistic Fermi gas)
\item Stiff nuclear reaction networks (alpha-chains, electron capture)
\item Radiation hydrodynamics \& neutrino transport (FLD, two-moment closures)
\end{enumerate}

Modular codes (MESA, HARM, IllinoisGRMHD) break down under extreme dynamic stress. The Sovereign
Architecture unifies these operators into a single tensor-processing pipeline enforcing exact
conservation, positivity, and constrained transport.

\section{Spacetime Geometry and Covariant Governing Equations}

\subsection{ADM 3+1 Spacetime Split}

\[
ds^{2}
= -\alpha^{2} dt^{2}
+ \gamma_{ij}(dx^{i} + \beta^{i} dt)(dx^{j} + \beta^{j} dt),
\]

where $\alpha$ is the lapse, $\beta^{i}$ the shift, and $\gamma_{ij}$ the spatial metric with
$\sqrt{-g} = \alpha\sqrt{\gamma}$.

\subsection{Relativistic Conservation Laws}

\[
\nabla_{\mu}(\rho u^{\mu}) = 0,
\qquad
\nabla_{\mu} T^{\mu\nu} = 0.
\]

\subsection{Magnetohydrodynamic Stress-Energy Tensor}

\[
T^{\mu\nu}
= (\rho h + b^{2})u^{\mu}u^{\nu}
+ \left(P + \frac{1}{2}b^{2}\right)g^{\mu\nu}
- b^{\mu}b^{\nu},
\]

with
\[
h = 1 + \epsilon + \frac{P}{\rho},
\qquad
b^{\mu} = \frac{1}{2}\epsilon^{\mu\nu\kappa\lambda}u_{\nu}F_{\kappa\lambda}.
\]

